,title,link,text,language,family
0,Western Dani language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Dani_language,"Western Dani, or Lani, is a Nuclear-Trans-New Guinea language. It is the Papuan language with the most speakers in Indonesian New Guinea. It is spoken by the Lani people in the province of Highland Papua. The Baliem Valley tribes are called Oeringoep and Timorini in literature from the 1920s, but those names are no longer used.","Dani, Western",Trans-New Guinea
1,Baliem Valley languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baliem_Valley_languages,"The Dani or Baliem Valley languages are a family of clearly related Trans–New Guinea languages spoken by the Dani and related peoples in the Baliem Valley in the Highland Papua, Indonesia.","Dani, Western",Trans-New Guinea
2,Trans–New Guinea languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trans–New_Guinea_languages,"Trans–New Guinea (TNG) is an extensive family of Papuan languages spoken on the island of New Guinea and neighboring islands, a region corresponding to the country Papua New Guinea as well as parts of Indonesia.","Dani, Western",Trans-New Guinea
3,"Dani, Western",https://accentnetwork.com/dani-western/,"Trans-New Guinea. Dani, Western, Indonesia. Dani Du: Voice of the Highlands.Western Dani, spoken by approximately 200,000 in Papua, Indonesia. Part of the Trans-New Guinea family. Market Insights. Content remains oral, with some regional radio.","Dani, Western",Trans-New Guinea
